{"title":"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Simple_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Simple Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀Just_4_min!🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀Just 4 min!🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A four-term sequence is formed by adding each term of a four-term arithmetic sequence of positive integers to the corresponding term of a four-term geometric sequence of positive integers. The first three terms of the resulting four-term sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b14ef560acadba8244952e9a8d5481f494445dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the fourth term of this sequence?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da4252f8d995c50d6c0569d944566fddd1893f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 190 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 194 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 198 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 202 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 206$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"446\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Algebra)\">Solution 1 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the arithmetic sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41b9e3ed2a79dc05a08a21dab15e80a944bf297c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,a+d,a+2d,a+3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" /> and the geometric sequence be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2ed566c1a34ab2e5b27a95f1e29795bfc99b4fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,br,br^2,br^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive number. We are given that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff745e3afedd46ee42d9fdfab7e4f8c662b2132.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a+b&amp;=57, \\\\ a+d+br&amp;=60, \\\\ a+2d+br^2&amp;=91, \\end{align*}\" width=\"142\" height=\"69\" />\nand we wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c73a0f1d4047c97ff3bc1676c453f4a5beac14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d+br^3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the first equation from the second and the second equation from the third, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a68e52d826ea6f3ce07f90e2cfa48615bf3c5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} d+b(r-1)&amp;=3, \\\\ d+br(r-1)&amp;=31. \\end{align*}\" width=\"147\" height=\"43\" />\nSubtracting these equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07fa69c659a238147f3428138ea735b90fd1c9e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b(r-1)^2=28.\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" />\nFrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a3797e796e728c7f60696d34df252297290d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+b(r-1)=3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b38fd17954523a9b91244a30bc778b45d4c8f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(r-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> is an integer. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/2315427eee9ba9a16c6f33f97319dd32194ad72d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(r-1)^2=28,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a33ca624def42acbaf86ea29772213251a46f01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2(r-1)^2=(b(r-1))^2=28b\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"20\" /> is a perfect square. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a1978d59be7c0253ad720eded79d10cd5868fe12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=7m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" /> From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14a9f423aed3641dc51f9818ad8d9f4f8894b65b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=57,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b944cad9ab1cbdc4cd695559ac8deb73ead41f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\leq56.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> Therefore, the only possibilities are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65f0a3d1e5510f00143236de4a310f38623fce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=28,7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68b301071c927eee78e8b693ab5296a27f76561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-1)^2=1,4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"21\" /> respectively. We proceed with casework:\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/4113effabae74aad01218d6aa2b271448341a08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-1)^2=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76e53988813de96bc1ab10621e3a23426b1c3a0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=2,b=28,a=29,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319c0588049053a6065fb57e2b2d4ae246803263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=-25.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> The arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1631176668923790ebcfeef0e2ad5c167c752424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29,4,-21,-46,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> which contradicts the positive-integer condition.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c6845df244d34f311d75d58b6da8810253ef8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-1)^2=4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07ffbf435b6a7a81e8fd068b96c616a25ba84797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=3,b=7,a=50,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94eeac937bb6b6be77c99dac1f0b5d7e9d49f278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=-11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> The arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8baf2095550bd7775513b22c530c6ef1dc8a8ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50,39,28,17,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" /> and the geometric sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a66d3ec376b19cdefb9b9d346d76bcae324118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,21,63,189.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" /> This case is valid.</li></ul>\n<p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13528ac391639118e4bdb86072942e36db3f2bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d+br^3=17+189=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 206}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"292\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy282 ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start similarly to Solution 1 and deduce the three equations\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/928d07a8a10223073d9a789526e4b677a92cb01e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a+b&amp;=57, \\\\ a+d+br&amp;=60, \\\\ a+2d+br^2&amp;=91. \\end{align*}\" width=\"142\" height=\"67\" />\nThen, add the last two equations and take away the first equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44de80aedd97b3eb67b93791354cd24e8770c230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d+br^2+br-b=94$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" />. We can solve for this in terms of what we want: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb45ba3896dac2a7bfac166d7aaf7c9d457a2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d=-br^2-br+b+94$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We're looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3adb74cbc3565b80e6831d553a274448f2f2efea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d+br^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />. We can substitute our value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05e574bb2b4ff8d69713613c435fabea7ec0d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> in here to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd667d015a73d0b0356c5523e6238899323eded1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[br^3-br^2-br+b+94=b(r+1)(r-1)(r-1)+94.\\]\" width=\"417\" height=\"20\" />\nSince our sequence only has positive integers we can now check by the answer choices. For each answer choice, we can subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698a90ad1ee1841d9c2a4a80e0a32cbd6b252181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$94$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and factor it to see if it has a perfect square factor and at least one other factor and those should differ by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde2c03870deb1daf64774916aca1e0ed315b41a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} \\textbf{(A)} \\ 190-94&amp;=96&amp;&amp;=2^5\\cdot3, \\\\ \\textbf{(B)} \\ 194-94&amp;=100&amp;&amp;=2^2\\cdot5^2, \\\\ \\textbf{(C)} \\ 198-94&amp;=104&amp;&amp;=2^3\\cdot13, \\\\ \\textbf{(D)} \\ 202-94&amp;=108&amp;&amp;=2^2\\cdot3^3, \\\\ \\textbf{(E)} \\ 206-94&amp;=112&amp;&amp;=2^4\\cdot7. \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"130\" />\nFrom this, the only possible answer choices are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31faa8c684ba5811ac60ea1bd0c855d8ef4d8b16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=3$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. To solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we look back to the given equations above.\n</p><p>We are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0f31f0ef8012646582dc86b08c3b5f114367a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3d+27b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> were the answer, then we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> would have to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> would equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Looking at our second equation, if this were the case, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would also have to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, this contradicts the third equation, as all variables are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but their sum isn't. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886bf9fb19e41584786f2ae785229b6c92886938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 206}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"74\" height=\"30\" /> is our answer.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Simple_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Simple_Algebra)\">Solution 3 (Simple Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Simple Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> be the first three terms of the geometric sequence.\n</p><p>Then the first three terms of the arithmetic sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/82568e36799d5e9070ef78d75fb5e0db83763bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d308a9fe2f707eb36b96a9251cbeb057571491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e46716a051855fb40ffbaa0a270ab6e97f407f07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since the arithmetic sequence has a constant difference, the first and third terms add up to twice the second term:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3bd3b885461fb1c7f347753518862f4a9b1ffab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(57-x)+(91-z)=2(60-y).\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/8730c46dcc74bd1d2e5ea273cfd3db868e0f158d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+z-2y=28.\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> form a geometric sequence, we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647c46622cc83d93deb066d01495990025601a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and substituting gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5b12e66315b5b476079ab5fbe80567721f1090.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2-2xy=28x,\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acad4b1044086356879c6deca84491a7b46f77f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-y)^2=28x.\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since the left side is a perfect square and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b14ef560acadba8244952e9a8d5481f494445dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the only possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7f6230166a491e7a471a03829c792496576480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c20fefe7f021988811f7c5ba12a061e0396a436.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(7-y)^2=196.\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd662d8cbd050d48a71ec7df8f99c22640527804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647c46622cc83d93deb066d01495990025601a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9be73953f10e853b5b35df1f5baaa519eec796.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z=\\frac{21^2}{7}=63.\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676c88bbf0f79f4170c0d13df2d3c49f45287ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=28$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2bf4289a4a282c209cdb87d741c3d81f6003fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(28-y)^2=784.\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed27dc23eb5b804966050e762b7dbd6628d4efed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>However, this gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d6f1b399486e6179f89ca24c29cac1d46d76c9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z=\\frac{56^2}{28}=112,\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>which is impossible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f2ebf0347d847a3e1eea17c96f85a62775e783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&lt;91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the geometric sequence must begin\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/288aec3ff36610aece91cc028ed98b60e3486c4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[7,\\ 21,\\ 63,\\ 189.\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the first three terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d342faf16864b2ec2f7e579aa43ba784d48c6b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57,60,91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />, the arithmetic sequence begins\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddadc0c604e4b79f10e1836a8e4b1450ba131049.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[50,\\ 39,\\ 28,\\ 17.\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Adding the fourth terms, we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d80b348640542996363384af0a5fc13450ba6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[17+189=\\boxed{206}.\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c182d936b9ff33cadf7f6e3391eeddf9248a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ Underscore_\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80Just_4_min.21.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀Just_4_min!🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀Just 4 min!🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀Just 4 min!🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/P13VHc26Sgo\">https://youtu.be/P13VHc26Sgo</a>\n~<i>Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DBHhSX8oVME\">https://youtu.be/DBHhSX8oVME</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A\">2022 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=